think Followed the ORDER clause: ran fleet_round_open.sh to settle HEAD before claiming, then fleet_claim.sh --open, staged both fleet-claims.kyri and ITINERARY.md, and pushed before building.
think The push raced three peer landings (pheromone's one_graph_dag_paper repair, two incense/petrichor session logs); rebased three times, resolving one real conflict in fleet-claims.kyri (pheromone's claim had already closed upstream) and re-amending the card's Git nib to HEAD's parent each time per rule 2.
think Proved the witness both ways on metal: present it reads GREEN at verdict=ok; with gratitude/ironbeetle moved aside and restored, it refuses with the named ABSENT message.
think Rostered the guard entry in standing-equipment.kyri, added the landed account to ITINERARY.md, and closed the claim with fleet_claim.sh --close, which carried the card's nib again.
obs The three-way rebase race is the ORDER clause's own lesson in miniature: a claim pushed promptly still meets a busy pier, and the twice-pulled discipline (fetch, rebase, re-amend) is what keeps the nib honest through it rather than the push succeeding on the first try.
